A||||22||MinnGreenGT||Friday night cruise at Porkey's!!!||||6||
Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||08-18-2001||01:51 AM||||Tonite (last night- whatever) a bunch of us gathered at Jimmy's house in Bloomington.  There 6 at Jimmy's and we picked up one more in St.Paul (sorry, I didn't grab names...tell us who you were!)  Anyway- we cruised up to Porky's, made a couple of quick passes, then parked at Arby's.  The lot was nearly full of import rides (bleah).  As we were standing around, the wind picked up something nasty- looked like rain at first, then turned out to be sand/dust- ouch.  As soon as the wind picked up, the imports all totally disappeared- guess they were afraid their big wings would catch the wind and their cars would fly away  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  We stood around and talked for awhile after moving our cars to the front of the lot (everyone left)- and then the rains came!  Standard departed, and the rest of us headed to the local Perkins to hang out some more.<P>Enough of my long-winded explanation (I had about 4 cups of coffe at Perkins).  Thanks to everyone who came!  To those who didn't- we're sorry you missed it and you'll have to join us next time.<P>As for the pics... it was dark and the flash on my digital didn't pick up a ton- so I dragged them through photoshop and these are what I came up with!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pkruse.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pkruse1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pkruse2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pkruse3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pkruse4.jpg"> <P>I may have a couple more...we'll see!<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg">  <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||6
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||08-18-2001||02:06 AM||||Ok... here's the other two. Yeah, I know the quality kinda sucks- but what can I say? It was dark and I was just freehand-shooting with a digital!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pkruse5.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pkruse6.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jimmy||08-18-2001||11:58 AM||||Nice pics!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Its too bad the dust came otherwise we could have checked out some more cars at Porky's.  Did anyone remember that civic hatch that got hard on the gas to spin his tires then suddenly had to lock up his brakes so he didn't hit one of his friends!  I LMAO!  We will have to try this again and hope for better weather. <P>Fierohoho, did you get home OK?<P>BTW Standards car is awesome!  Sharp lookin car.  Pherder built a cool Fiero,  I'm glad Standard was able to buy it.<P>Jim<BR>87 GT<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierohoho||08-18-2001||12:24 PM||||It was a great evening everyone, I had a good time.<P>After I left Perkins I drove by Porky's and saw two white Fieros so I pulled in, Uaana and Matt Kneen with his '84 500ci V-8 Indy.<P>I didn't stay long, just enough to say hi and take another look at Matt's car.<P>I stopped by Tina's shop on the way home and there were no lights on, Tina did you get the clutch done?<P>By the time I got home it was pushing 1:30am and still raining, I had a grand total of 190 miles for the trip this time, wow! sore butt city.<P>Great pics MinnGreenGT, thats me secong from the left in the first pic.<P>Why is it I always park opposite of everyone, nice pics of all the cars and there's my dull '84 the only one in line backwards, a little help next time please? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Until next time, Fierohoho <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||08-18-2001||07:50 PM||||If was fun guys!  I hope I can do it again.. got some bad news...<P>I think I spun a bearing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Car felt fine all the way home, get into my garage and I heard a little more clatter than usual coming from the back.  Ducked under the car and oooooooooo #$&*(#%  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> sounds like a bunch of rocks flying around in the oil pan.  Only at idle, though.  Still pulls fine, though I havne't pushed it.  Oil pressure is still up..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Anybody got any sources for a HO quad 4?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jimmy||08-18-2001||08:59 PM||||Damn Standard, rotten luck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  How hard is it to take the oil pan off of a quad four?  LMK if you need help with anything.  Maybe a good time to invest in some speed parts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Jim<BR>87 GT<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||08-18-2001||09:16 PM||||Ya I'm just hoping it doesn't blow up anytime soon.  <P>I'm thinking it would probably be easiest to find another running quad 4 HO and pull a quick remove & replace.  Or else just try my luck and replace the bearings with the quad in the car...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tina||08-19-2001||12:09 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>I stopped by Tina's shop on the way home and there were no lights on, Tina did you get the clutch done?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>We must of just missed us.<BR>Well,didn't get started until like around 8PM.<BR>(Too many customer cars,Uaana being one of them   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<BR>Then ended running out of steam around 1AM.<P>BUT, the new clutch is in now, everything else back together.<BR>3 cans of engine decreaser later, engine looks great again, me on the other side...<BR>don't operate a airhose when almost   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"> <P>Anyways, the whole thing is going back in this afternoon.<BR>Can't wait.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Until next time, Fierohoho   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>[/b]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Let me know when and where.<P>Tina<BR>BTW Standard, ....that is too bad.<p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||08-19-2001||02:36 PM||||Preliminary good (very good) news!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Seems all that noise was coming from the exhaust system.. the cat was really close to the frame rail in back, and it seems all those huge (really huge!) puddles I went through on the highway friday night shoved it back a bit, so it rattles against the frame rail.  May have killed the cat, too.. seems to be a bit of rattling coming from inside it.  After I bent it away the "knock" disappeared.  Still have to take it for a drive and see if I get the same results when the oil is hot, but I think we're going to be alright!  woohoo!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Also explains why it would stop when the engine was under load.. it would torque back and hold the cat against the frame rail.  Then when I stoped and idle'd it would rattle like crazy.. I need to get some more support for the exhaust.. hmmmm.. of course, i could also just get rid of the cat and that loop of exhaust and make a straight shot from the manifold right to the muffler  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||1
